<article class="env-remark" id="03P6">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03P6">Remark <span data-tag="03P6">59.23.4</span>.</a> In the terminology introduced above a special case of Theorem <a href="/tag/03P2" data-tag="03P2">59.22.4</a> is </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  H_{fppf}^ p(X, \mathbf{G}_ a) = H_{\acute{e}tale}^ p(X, \mathbf{G}_ a) = H_{Zar}^ p(X, \mathbf{G}_ a) = H^ p(X, \mathcal{O}_ X)  \]
</div>
  <p> for all $p \geq 0$. Moreover, we could use the notation $H^ p_{fppf}(X, \mathcal{O}_ X)$ to indicate the cohomology of the structure sheaf on the big fppf site of $X$. </p>
</article>